# The partner repositories molpack is built against. CI checks the same
# repository and ref out with setup-partners in .github/workflows
# (repository MolCrafts/molrs, ref dev, path ../molrs). This file must name
# that same repository and ref. `partners.py run` is the relock recipe below.
# A local build uses the sibling ../molrs as it is.
#
# KEY=VALUE lines only. SELF is this repository's directory name.
#
# On dev the ref is molrs's dev. The workflow names that ref; it does not
# look up a same-named branch. A release commit on master sets this file's
# MOLRS_REF and the workflow `ref` to the molrs release tag of the line
# Cargo.toml names.
#
# Cargo.lock, python/Cargo.lock and python/uv.lock record molrs's package
# metadata (its version and dependencies), not a commit. When molrs's dev
# changes that metadata the lock gates fail; relock in a commit of its own:
#   scripts/partners.py run -- sh -c 'cargo update -w && (cd python && cargo update -w && uv lock) \
#     && cp Cargo.lock "$PARTNERS_SOURCE/" && cp python/Cargo.lock python/uv.lock "$PARTNERS_SOURCE/python/"'
SELF=molpack
MOLRS_REPOSITORY=MolCrafts/molrs
MOLRS_REF=dev
